infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Brand the type, or leave it a plain string?
  desc Typecheck cost is noise; the real price is boundary friction
  compares
    - label Brand the primitive
      children
        - label Catches swapped ids at compile time
          desc OrderId cannot pass where a UserId is wanted
        - label Adds under 100ms to typecheck
          desc On a ~7.2s tsc --noEmit baseline (~1,200 .ts files): noise
        - label ~40 boundary casts in the first PR
          desc asUserId(...) at every JSON.parse, ORM row, URL param
        - label Reserve for ids, money, validated input
          desc Where a swapped value is a production incident
    - label Leave plain string
      children
        - label Zero boundary friction
          desc Structural typing as designed — no casts anywhere
        - label JSON.parse / ORM / URL just flow
          desc Values arrive as plain string, no wrapping step
        - label Swapped ids compile silently
          desc The bug class you accept in exchange
        - label Right for ordinary domain objects
          desc Branding costs more than the bug it prevents
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
